Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.38,0:00:07.30,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,450,5540,5900)\pos(653.755,349.455)}Episode 68
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.38,0:00:08.26,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,450,5540,5900)\pos(653.755,539.788)}The Northern Expedition
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.46,0:00:24.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi died of illness. The following year, his son Cao Rui ascended to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.10,0:00:29.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhong Yao was appointed as Grand Tutor, Cao Zhen as the Grand General,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.26,0:00:32.46,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and Cao Xiu as the Minister of War.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.94,0:00:37.46,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Hua Xin was appointed as Grand Commandant, Wang Lang as the Minister over the Masses,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.94,0:00:40.14,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Chen Qun as Minister of Works,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.66,0:00:43.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and Sima Yi as the Grand General of Fast Cavalry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.10,0:00:47.98,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Xiliang (西凉): Modern day Gansu province, to the west of Chang'an.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.02,0:00:47.98,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Sima Yi petitioned to guard the western regions of Liang.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.78,0:00:48.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(312,450)}Cáo Ruì\NStyled: Yuánzhòng
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.38,0:00:54.46,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Rui then appointed him as Governor, granting him command of the troops of Yong and Liang Provinces.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.66,0:00:59.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3700,3980)\pos(324,326)}Sīmǎ Yì\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.78,0:01:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi is dead, and Cao Rui has ascended to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.54,0:01:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,While the other courtiers are not to be worried about, Sima Yi possesses a keen tactical mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.78,0:01:14.90,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4700,5100)\pos(312,350)}Mǎ Sù\NStyled: Yòucháng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.18,0:01:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,He did not stay in the court of Xuchang.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.86,0:01:21.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4340,4740)\pos(973,465)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.02,0:01:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, he went to command the troops of Yong and Liang Provinces.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.74,0:01:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He has greater plans in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.74,0:01:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If the armies of Yong and Liang are well trained,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.18,0:01:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,they will be a major threat to the Shu army. \NIt is better to attack them first.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.58,0:01:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.02,0:01:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You have just returned from the south. \NThe troops are weary and need rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.26,0:01:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,A long expedition is inadvisable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.30,0:01:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.50,0:01:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, if you used one plan instead of an army,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.54,0:02:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sima Yi could die in the hands of Cao Rui himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.58,0:02:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The threat would be removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.42,0:02:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What good plan do you have? Please do share it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.74,0:02:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Though Sima Yi is a major Wei official,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.42,0:02:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Rui has always been suspicious of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.90,0:02:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not send people in secrecy to Luoyang, Ye Commandery, and other places,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.14,0:02:26.26,Default,,0,0,0,,spreading rumors that he intends to rebel?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.54,0:02:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.86,0:02:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, place announcements in the name of Sima Yi in multiple places
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.26,0:02:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,as evidence of his treason.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.10,0:03:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I, Sima Yi, General of Agile Cavalry, Commander of the Yong, Liang, and other provincial armies,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.34,0:03:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}hereby proclaim in good faith...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.78,0:03:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}...Imperial Grandson Cao Rui, devoid of moral conduct,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.14,0:03:11.42,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Taizu (太祖): Temple name meaning "Great Ancestor," referring to Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.10,0:03:11.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}has been enthroned in violation of Emperor Taizu's last will.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.62,0:03:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Today, I, by the grace of Heaven and men, shall raise troops
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.38,0:03:19.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}to appease all the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.06,0:03:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}From now on, everyone is to pledge allegiance to the new sovereign.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.18,0:03:22.86,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,According to the original text of the novel, this person is Cao Zhi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.74,0:03:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Those who do not shall have their entire clan executed!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.74,0:03:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Sima Yi dares to install a new emperor?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.98,0:03:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, this must be a\N fabrication by Shu and Wu agents
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.42,0:03:37.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3820,4140)\pos(320,448)}Cáo Zhēn\NStyled: Zǐdān
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.90,0:03:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,so that they could attack while our court is in chaos.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.62,0:03:44.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty must tread carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.58,0:03:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}I disagree.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.18,0:03:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}In the past, Martial Emperor Taizu said to me:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.78,0:03:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,664)}"Sima Yi has the eyes of eagles and wolves."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.90,0:03:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}"He must not command armies."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.82,0:03:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}"He shall bring chaos to the realm."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.02,0:03:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}This man must be removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.66,0:04:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,If Shu and Wu take advantage of \Nthe chaos and attack, what then?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.10,0:04:04.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(332,474)}Huà Xīn\NStyled: Zǐyú
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.02,0:04:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we defend if we have rebellions?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.42,0:04:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know that Sima Yi is a threat?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.42,0:04:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The notice is here; his heart is clear!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.58,0:04:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,A piece of notice is no proof!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.78,0:04:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, beloved ministers, no need to quarrel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.22,0:04:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,There is no proof, but we \Nshould still prepare in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.94,0:04:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Beloved ministers, what plans would you suggest?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.10,0:04:25.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.54,0:04:29.66,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Liu Bang (刘邦), Emperor Gaozu of Han (汉高祖), suspecting General Han Xin's (韩信) disloyalty, pretended to tour the Yunmeng Marshes (云梦泽) to arrest Han Xin, though he later pardoned him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.02,0:04:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Should you be suspicious,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.38,0:04:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}you could mimic Han Gaozu's stratagem of pretending to tour Yunmeng, and visit Anyi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.02,0:04:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Sima Yi will come to greet you. \NObserve his reaction,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.46,0:04:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and he can be captured in front of the chariot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.90,0:04:45.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A good plan. We shall go there with the imperial guards.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.22,0:04:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us see what his reaction will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.14,0:05:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Report! His Majesty announces his intent to come to Anyi for an inspection.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.14,0:05:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The Son of Heaven must be coming to Anyi to inspect our troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.66,0:05:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, the armies must be well-dressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.62,0:05:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Line up outside the city to welcome him and show our might.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.30,0:05:28.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.78,0:05:42.54,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, Sima Yi is leading over a hundred thousand troops!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.54,0:05:45.38,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He means to defend himself! He is clearly rebelling!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.50,0:05:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, do not be alarmed!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.02,0:05:51.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me lead the troops to hold him accountable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.62,0:05:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,If he rebels, execute him without mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.02,0:05:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.34,0:06:04.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The Emperor is coming, prepare to welcome him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.46,0:06:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda, you were entrusted by the late emperor himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.62,0:06:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Why have you raised troops against us?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.30,0:06:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Wenlie, why do you say this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.46,0:06:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The Sima family is indebted to the Emperor's grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.42,0:06:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I raise my arms in rebellion?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.18,0:06:30.82,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4300,4620)\pos(316,450)}Cáo Xiū\NStyled: Wénliè
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.06,0:06:30.62,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have no ulterior motives, \Nwhy lead all these soldiers here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.22,0:06:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your intention is clear!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.78,0:06:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Wenlie, this is all but a misunderstanding!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.34,0:06:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I brought the army to welcome the Son of Heaven,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.78,0:06:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,to strengthen His Majesty's prestige!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.18,0:06:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,See for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.34,0:07:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,This is just a scheme by Wu and Shu agents to sow discord.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.74,0:07:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,They want us to fight each other so that they can take advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.54,0:07:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go see His Majesty and clarify this matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.94,0:07:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Men!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.86,0:07:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.30,0:07:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Withdraw to camp!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.90,0:07:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.30,0:07:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.30,0:07:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I was entrusted by the late Martial Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.18,0:07:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I dare harbor treason?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.14,0:07:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,This is just a scheme by Wu and Shu agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.50,0:07:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I request a division of troops to first defeat Shu and then attack Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.22,0:07:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,to repay your generosity and prove my loyalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.26,0:08:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.06,0:08:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, truth and lies are hard to tell apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.62,0:08:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He cannot be given power. \NDismiss him and send him back to his hometown.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.82,0:08:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,If you, sir, have no rebellious intentions,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.54,0:08:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We will not pursue this matter further.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.94,0:08:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.22,0:08:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}As you have commanded much and rested little,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.50,0:08:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}we hereby appoint Cao Xiu as \Ncommander of the Yong and Liang armies,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.58,0:08:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}in your stead!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.98,0:08:37.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.38,0:08:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}You may resign and return home to recuperate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.50,0:08:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.10,0:08:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.06,0:09:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your Majesty, now that the Wei lord Cao Pi is dead, Cao Rui has only recently been enthroned,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.54,0:09:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and the army commander of Yong and Liang, Sima Yi, has now been dismissed and sent home,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.70,0:09:18.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(641.333,665.333)}this is a Heaven-sent chance to strike at Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.14,0:09:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I hope that Your Majesty may \Nallow me the task of marching north,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.66,0:09:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}recovering the Central Plains \Nand accomplishing our great cause!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.58,0:09:24.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Go. Go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.38,0:09:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You go first. Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.62,0:09:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go first!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.42,0:09:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.90,0:09:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, what is the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.82,0:09:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I request to march north against Wei, \Nto restore the Han Dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.14,0:10:02.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5940,6380)\pos(316,453)}Liú Shàn\NStyled: Gōngsì
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.78,0:10:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, Cao-Wei is far away in Luoyang and has not invaded our borders.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.70,0:10:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We are at peace now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.94,0:10:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This is what We have long desired.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.94,0:10:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, you have just returned from the south and have suffered much.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.54,0:10:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Why must you leave Us again?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.06,0:10:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We truly cannot bear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.22,0:10:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The restoration of the Han dynasty
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.34,0:10:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,is the last will of the late emperor and Your Majesty's great cause.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.38,0:10:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Wei traitors are not eliminated, I will not be able to rest peacefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.98,0:10:37.66,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I disappoint the late emperor's heavy trust?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.66,0:10:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.34,0:10:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,With you by Our side, Chancellor, We can rest easy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.02,0:10:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,So We do not wish for Father-Chancellor to go far away!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.42,0:10:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,As for the northern expedition... \NLet's talk about it another day, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.18,0:10:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Court dismissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.34,0:10:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.14,0:11:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, go back home early to rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.98,0:11:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not overexert yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.54,0:11:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.50,0:11:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Bite, bite it! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.38,0:11:37.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Bite, quick, good!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.22,0:11:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I have long waited to attack Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.90,0:11:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Fortunately, Sima Yi has\N been demoted due to our trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.26,0:12:01.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Time waits for no one, or I would regret it for life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.62,0:12:28.50,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}Memorial on Expedition
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.62,0:12:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Your subject, Liang, writes to you:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.42,0:12:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The late emperor passed away \Nbefore fulfilling his great undertaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.70,0:12:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Now, the world is divided into three,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.02,0:12:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and with Yi Province in dire straits, this is indeed a critical moment...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.02,0:13:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}By valuing worthy men and \Ndistancing itself from wicked men,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.82,0:13:11.26,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Former Han: Alternative name of Western Han Dynasty (202 BCE - 9 CE)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.74,0:13:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}the Former Han prospered.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.06,0:13:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}By valuing wicked men and \Ndistancing itself from worthy men,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.82,0:13:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}the Later Han was brought to ruin.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.42,0:13:16.26,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Later Han: Alternative name of Eastern Han Dynasty (25 CE - 220 CE).
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.78,0:13:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I, once a common man, toiled in my fields in Nanyang,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.26,0:13:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}doing what I could to survive in a time of chaos
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.98,0:13:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and taking no interest in fame and titles.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.14,0:13:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}The late emperor, not minding my lesser station,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.90,0:13:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}humbled himself and thrice visited my thatched cottage,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.90,0:13:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}consulting me about world affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.90,0:13:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}I, in great gratitude, placed myself into his service.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.98,0:13:49.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}As calamity followed, I took command of a defeated army,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.94,0:13:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and received this task\N during a time of great peril.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.54,0:13:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Now, twenty-one years have passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.98,0:14:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}The late emperor knew that I am cautious,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.78,0:14:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}so he entrusted me with this great endeavor before his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.06,0:14:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Since then, my mind has been troubled day and night,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.98,0:14:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}fearing I could not live up to his expectations and thus discredit his judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.18,0:14:18.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Thus, I crossed the Lu River in the fifth month, entering deep into the wilderness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.90,0:14:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Now with the south pacified \Nand the armies ready,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.82,0:14:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}I shall lead the army, strike the Central Plains,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.50,0:14:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and exhaust every means to remove the traitors,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.34,0:14:30.50,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Former capital: Chang'an (Western Han) and Luoyang (Eastern Han).
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.26,0:14:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}restore the Han Dynasty, \Nand return it to its former capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.06,0:14:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}That is how I shall repay the late emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.62,0:14:37.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and fulfill my duty to Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.58,0:14:45.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I hope that Your Majesty grant me \Nthe order to suppress the traitors,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.94,0:14:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and punish me should I prove unfit
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.70,0:14:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}so that the late emperor's soul may be at rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.54,0:14:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your Majesty should take counsel with yourself to seek the right path,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.18,0:15:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}examine and adopt sound thoughts, \Nand forever honor the late emperor's last edict.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.46,0:15:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}I, your minister, will be forever grateful!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.94,0:15:12.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Now that I must leave, I weep next to this petition,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.30,0:15:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}not knowing what to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.46,0:15:28.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, you have fought many battles south and north without rest,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.18,0:15:31.10,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and you have only now just returned to the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.70,0:15:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that you want to go on a northern \Nexpedition, We fear it will be too taxing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.42,0:15:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I, entrusted by the late emperor with his heir, have never neglected this duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.22,0:15:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With the south pacified, any internal troubles are no more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.78,0:15:50.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}If now is not the time to defeat the traitors and restore the Central Plains, then when will be?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.50,0:15:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Your Majesty, I have observed the night sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.66,0:16:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The northern sky is bound by vigor, its stars brimming with light.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.86,0:16:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Cao-Wei is not to be attacked.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.58,0:16:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Chancellor, you are well-versed in astronomy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.50,0:16:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Why be forceful?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.06,0:16:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}The ways of Heaven are capricious.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.90,0:16:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}How can we rely on it only?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.34,0:16:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}I shall garrison in Hanzhong and act accordingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.34,0:16:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your Majesty, the northern expedition must not be done!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.54,0:16:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Our Han Empire is remote.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.66,0:16:33.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}With a scarcity of generals and strength,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.86,0:16:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}we cannot contend with Cao-Wei for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.98,0:16:41.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Furthermore, the mountains to the north are treacherous,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.06,0:16:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}easy to defend, difficult to attack, and hard to supply.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.06,0:16:46.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Managing the army will be impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.90,0:16:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}This is a major military taboo!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.42,0:16:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}The ancients have said:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.42,0:16:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}"A gentleman ought to know \Nnot doing what cannot be done."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.62,0:17:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I earnestly beseech Your Majesty to consider this well!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.82,0:17:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Your Majesty, throughout military history,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.62,0:17:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}defeating many with few and defeating \Nstrength with weakness can oft be found.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.58,0:17:14.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Have you, Court Counselor, \Nforgotten about the Battle of Chibi?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.70,0:17:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}Your Majesty, should you miss this chance,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.54,0:17:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}and take refuge in only one corner of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.94,0:17:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}how long could such a refuge last?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.26,0:17:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}If I cannot repay the late emperor's grace and his trust,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.38,0:17:38.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord14}my life would be worse than death!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.46,0:17:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Since Father-Chancellor insists on sending troops, We will comply.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.82,0:17:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,But who will take charge of affairs in the court after you leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.78,0:17:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, rest assured. I have already made arrangements.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.18,0:18:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Guo Youzhi, Dong Yun, and \NFei Yi will be Palace-Attendants.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.18,0:18:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Take charge of palace affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.98,0:18:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.06,0:18:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiang Chong will oversee the Imperial Guards.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.26,0:18:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chen Zhen will be Attendant, \N Jiang Wan will be Adjutant,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.22,0:18:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and Zhang Yi will be the Chief Clerk,\N handling the affairs of the Chancellor's office.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.26,0:18:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,All civil and military officials will work together to manage affairs of the land of Shu without negligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.06,0:18:18.46,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1980,2380)\pos(1000,492)}Qiáo Zhōu\NStyled: Yǔnnán
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.38,0:18:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.94,0:18:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please issue a decree to allow me to raise troops for the northern expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.06,0:18:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Issue the decree!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.74,0:18:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.26,0:18:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.42,0:18:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zilong.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.46,0:18:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.38,0:19:00.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, though I am old,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.54,0:19:03.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5260,5620)\pos(993,470)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.26,0:19:06.58,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Lian Po (廉頗, died 243 BCE): General of Zhao, one of the Warring States.\NMa Yuan (马援, died 49 CE): General of Eastern Han Dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.26,0:19:03.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I still have the courage of Lian Po \Nand the valor of Ma Yuan.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.10,0:19:05.74,Default,,0,0,0,,They did not submit to their old age.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.90,0:19:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, for this northern expedition, why do you overlook me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.98,0:19:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong, when I returned to the capital from the south, Ma Chao passed away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.98,0:19:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I deeply regret it, as if losing an arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.18,0:19:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.86,0:19:23.42,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General, you are older now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.42,0:19:26.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,If something happened to you, \Nit would harm your reputation
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.98,0:19:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,and diminish the morale of the Shu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.06,0:19:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, ever since I followed the late emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.78,0:19:35.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I have led on the frontlines, \Nnever retreating from peril.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.02,0:19:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It is a great honor for a man to die on the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.30,0:19:44.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, I am willing to be the vanguard of the army!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.98,0:19:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong, this northern expedition to \Nthe Central Plains will be dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.38,0:19:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.06,0:19:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.30,0:20:01.86,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not let me be the vanguard,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.86,0:20:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd rather smash my head on the steps and die here!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.78,0:20:08.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.66,0:20:15.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, if you wish to be the vanguard, you must take one person with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.70,0:20:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Who?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.42,0:20:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.70,0:20:26.50,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3500,3780)\pos(306,450)}Dèng Zhī\NStyled: Bómiáo
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.78,0:20:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I, though not talented, am willing to go with the Elder General to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.70,0:20:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Deng Zhi is willing to\N accompany me. What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.38,0:20:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Assign five thousand elite troops. Let Bomiao lead the charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.46,0:20:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.30,0:20:50.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass my order!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.70,0:20:52.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Onwards, to the north!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.90,0:21:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, urgent news from the border.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.50,0:21:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang is leading an army of 300,000 out of Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.78,0:21:22.70,Default,,0,0,0,,With Zhao Yun and Deng Zhi as the vanguard, they are violating our border!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.82,0:21:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Ministers, who will repel the Shu army?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.82,0:21:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.86,0:21:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,My father died in Hanzhong.\N I have not avenged the bitter grudge.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.86,0:21:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that Shu is invading,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.38,0:21:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I can lead the fiercest warriors!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.54,0:21:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I request Your Majesty to grant me command of the troops,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.82,0:21:50.66,Default,,0,0,0,,so that I may serve my nation and avenge my father!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.66,0:21:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,This must not be done!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.90,0:21:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, Prince Consort Xiahou has never seen combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.34,0:22:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Granting him such a heavy task is improper.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.06,0:22:04.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(324,472)}Wáng Lǎng\NStyled: Jǐngxīng
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.82,0:22:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Moreover, Zhuge Liang is a \Nmaster tactician, well-versed in strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.98,0:22:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,He is not to be underestimated.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.86,0:22:11.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Minister Wang, are you colluding with Zhuge Liang as an agent?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.70,0:22:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,How-How could this be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.46,0:22:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.62,0:22:20.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I studied the techniques of war from my father when I was young.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.02,0:22:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet you dare look down on me?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.22,0:22:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear I will not return without Zhuge Liang captured!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.34,0:22:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,-Your Majesty!\N-Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.86,0:22:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Beloved ministers, no need to quarrel.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.70,0:22:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The Prince Consort shall be made Chief Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.90,0:22:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall assign 200,000 troops west of the Tong Pass to repel Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.58,0:22:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.10,0:22:54.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3500,3900)\pos(998.667,432)}Xiàhóu Mào \NStyled: Zixiū
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.30,0:23:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.22,0:23:06.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, I heard that Zhuge Liang is invading.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.14,0:23:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess who that little Emperor Cao Rui-
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.70,0:23:16.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5600,5940)\pos(993,329)}Sīmǎ Zhāo\NStyled: Zǐshàng
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.50,0:23:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, guess who His Majesty the \NEmperor appointed as the Chief Commander?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.98,0:23:19.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Great General Cao Zhen?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.74,0:23:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.82,0:23:28.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6000,6460)\pos(940,460)}Sīmǎ Yì\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.86,0:23:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Minister of War Cao Xiu?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.38,0:23:26.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.34,0:23:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Then who...?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.86,0:23:33.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Prince Consort Xiahou Mao!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.30,0:23:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Him!?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.14,0:23:40.54,Default,,0,0,0,,How can he lead?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.78,0:23:43.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Why worry about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.58,0:23:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter who is the Commander, it's none of our business.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.70,0:23:49.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.86,0:23:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Mao is a useless lout.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.26,0:23:57.86,Default,,0,0,0,,How can he resist Zhuge Liang?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.74,0:24:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord is in grave danger!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.02,0:24:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, as Confucius saith, "If what in name is improper, then its meaning is dishonest."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.86,0:24:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, you have already stepped down.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.18,0:24:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You are no different from a commoner.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.26,0:24:38.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What use is writing a petition?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.14,0:24:56.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Mao, leading 200,000 troops \Nwest of Tong Pass, is coming to fight us.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.34,0:25:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The Wei vanguard Han De, along with his four sons and 80,000 troops,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.34,0:25:03.10,Default,,0,0,0,,is moving to Mount Fengming.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.10,0:25:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Send orders to Generals Zhao Yun and Deng Zhi:
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.46,0:25:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Intercept them at Fengming Mountain to ensure victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.02,0:25:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.74,0:25:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.02,0:25:18.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Han De and his sons are fierce and ruthless.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.82,0:25:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Zhao Yun is nearly seventy years of age. He might not be able to defeat them.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.90,0:25:31.10,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He insisted on being the vanguard. His loyalty and bravery are unwavering. Worry not.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.94,0:25:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, the northern expedition must be swift, not slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.70,0:25:39.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4940,5300)\pos(982,478)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.50,0:25:39.02,Default,,0,0,0,,If it drags on, it will be detrimental to our army.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.90,0:25:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Wenchang, what do you propose?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.66,0:25:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, I am willing to lead five thousand elite troops
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.62,0:25:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,to march east of the Qinling Mountains, through Ziwu Valley, and head north.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.02,0:25:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Within ten days, I can reach Chang'an.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.30,0:25:58.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You can march through Xie Valley to Xianyang.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.10,0:26:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, victory is assured.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.42,0:26:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not a foolproof plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.78,0:26:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Wei strategists anticipate it,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.18,0:26:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,they could set an ambush in the mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.90,0:26:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only will your five thousand men be in danger,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.34,0:26:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,but our entire army will also suffer.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.82,0:26:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Choosing the route concerns the entire operation and requires careful consideration.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.06,0:26:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, it is not that I underestimate the Wei army,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.74,0:26:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,but that Xiahou Mao is a pampered nobleman.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.34,0:26:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Though a Prince Consort, \Nhe lacks courage and wisdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.30,0:26:38.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That Cao Rui whelp has made such an incompetent man the Commander of the three armies.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.74,0:26:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Heaven aiding our success.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.22,0:26:45.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, this opportunity must not be missed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.38,0:26:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I will take the route through Longyou, marching on flat roads.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.66,0:26:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It is stable and safe. How can we not win?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.06,0:27:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I avoid taking any risks.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.38,0:27:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, to take a detour, to go afar than nearby... that...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.94,0:27:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,That... that... is not in line with...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.62,0:27:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The idea of achieving victory through surprise!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.54,0:27:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,My mind is made up. Do not say more.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.34,0:27:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.62,0:27:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.58,0:28:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhao Yun is almost seventy, yet still serves as vanguard.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.02,0:28:04.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3100,3380)\pos(878,276)}Hán Dé
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.06,0:28:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Are they mocking us of the Central Plains?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.66,0:28:11.82,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(344,211)}Hán Yīng
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.34,0:28:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, let my brothers and I capture him
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.22,0:28:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and destroy his reputation!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.78,0:28:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.78,0:28:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes! Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.98,0:28:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Who goes there? State your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.14,0:28:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Han Ying, eldest son of Han De, here to send you to your grave!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.46,0:28:29.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You are young, yet you come to seek death?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.02,0:28:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.30,0:28:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Qi, my son!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.66,0:28:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Are such paltry skills fit for a warrior?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.58,0:28:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,-Father.\N-Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.02,0:28:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Qiong, my son!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.94,0:29:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Who else dares to fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.78,0:29:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat, hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.98,0:29:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.22,0:29:39.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General, at seventy, you are as valiant as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.02,0:29:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You defeated four warriors in that clash, a rare feat!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.34,0:29:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor did not employ me due to my age,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.42,0:29:48.58,Default,,0,0,0,,so I had to prove myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.90,0:29:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, escort Han Yao and report this victory to the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.26,0:29:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, sir.\N-Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.54,0:30:00.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My small win today is not worth mentioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.30,0:30:03.26,Default,,0,0,0,,When that Xiahou Mao comes, I will capture him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.10,0:30:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou whelp, come and face your death!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.22,0:30:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, this man killed my \Nfour sons, I have not avenged them!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.18,0:30:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, let me fight him.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.98,0:30:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhao Yun, prepare to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.38,0:30:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,General Han!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.14,0:30:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat now!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.82,0:30:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.66,0:30:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I did not expect such a defeat today!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.02,0:30:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew about Zhao Yun,\N but have never seen him in person!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.50,0:31:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,That battle...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.58,0:31:06.30,Default,,0,0,0,,...proved that the stories of the Battle of Changban are indeed true!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.06,0:31:10.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed true!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.62,0:31:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,At this rate, no one can defeat him.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.66,0:31:20.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What should we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.10,0:31:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, Zhao Yun is strong but\N lacks strategy, he is not to be feared.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.06,0:31:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, engage him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.18,0:31:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Set an ambush along the mountain path.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.26,0:31:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,After the battle begins,\N retreat first and lure Zhao Yun.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.70,0:31:36.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Scale the mountain and direct from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.70,0:31:39.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,We will surround Zhao Yun, surely capturing him!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.86,0:31:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Splendid!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.22,0:31:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, we must lure him into the trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.90,0:32:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhao, be cautious of the Wei army's tricks. Be on guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.94,0:32:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,A mere boy, how can he be a threat?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.78,0:32:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I will capture him alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.66,0:33:01.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.78,0:33:11.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.54,0:33:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.34,0:33:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Release!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.66,0:33:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Loose the arrows!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.66,0:34:06.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not give into old age! I will die here today!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.14,0:34:15.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, look, another force is coming to attack us.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.54,0:34:18.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, over there too.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.86,0:34:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.06,0:34:29.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(385.6,422.4)}Zhāng Bāo
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.78,0:34:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat! Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.86,0:34:41.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General, the Chancellor feared for you, so he sent me to assist you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.10,0:34:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Good nephew, let us assault the enemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.02,0:34:44.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.82,0:34:58.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(342,433)}Guān Xīng\NStyled: Ānguó
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.94,0:34:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Zhao, the Chancellor sent me to assist you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.02,0:35:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.82,0:35:13.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,During Zhuge Liang's first northern expedition, \Nthe vanguard Zhao Yun, still strong in his old age,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.82,0:35:17.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,defeated Xiahou Mao in three successive battles, crushing him.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.30,0:35:21.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Mao fled to Nan'an Commandery, holding the fort and not coming out.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.10,0:35:25.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhao Yun and other generals attacked the city for days without success.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.38,0:35:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Mao is staying inside the fort.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.74,0:35:31.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Our army attacked the city \Nseveral times without success.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.42,0:35:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,This city has deep moats and high walls, difficult to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.62,0:35:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,If we only focus on besieging it, it will cost us time.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.14,0:35:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The Wei army could split up and take Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.06,0:35:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Our army would be in danger.\NWe must come up with another plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.30,0:35:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.42,0:35:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Mao is a Prince Consort of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.82,0:36:02.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6600,7100)\pos(939,470)}Dèng Zhī\NStyled: Bómiáo
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.22,0:36:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Capturing him is worth more\N than killing a hundred generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.10,0:36:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,We have him trapped in the city now.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.82,0:36:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we give up and not attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.46,0:36:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The city connects to Tianshui in the west and Anding in the north,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.58,0:36:14.90,Default,,0,0,0,,forming a strategic triangle.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.90,0:36:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,If we attack one city, will the other \Ntwo cities in the northwest do nothing?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.18,0:36:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,If they send soldiers to attack our rear,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.74,0:36:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,our army would not be able to take care of both ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.94,0:36:30.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Then what does the Chancellor suggest?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.26,0:36:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The city must be taken \Nthrough subterfuge, not force.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.98,0:36:38.74,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, outside the city of Nan'an Commandery,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.74,0:36:41.58,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,order firewood to be piled under their walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.58,0:36:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Claim that our army is going to burn the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.54,0:36:50.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Feign an attack on Nan'an to lure out the soldiers of Anding and Tianshui.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.34,0:36:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, our army will set an ambush halfway,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.58,0:36:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,destroy them, and seize the two commanderies.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.18,0:37:01.98,Default,,0,0,0,,With the two commanderies lost, how can the isolated Nan'an protect itself?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.18,0:37:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If the two commanderies of Tianshui and Anding
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.18,0:37:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,send no troops to rescue, what would we do then?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.38,0:37:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The Administrator of Tianshui, \NMa Zun, and the Administrator of Anding, Cui Liang
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.98,0:37:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,are both brave and loyal men.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.94,0:37:20.02,Default,,0,0,0,,With the Prince Consort trapped, how could they not rescue him?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.42,0:37:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There is no need to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.46,0:37:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Officers, tomorrow morning, wait for orders in front of the tent.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.10,0:37:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.06,0:37:36.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3900,4220)\pos(331,344)}Cuī Liàng
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.46,0:37:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Administrator Cui.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.82,0:37:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The Commander ordered me to break through the siege to send a message,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.46,0:37:42.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4860,5180)\pos(977,436)}Péi Xù
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.98,0:37:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,urging you to send troops to rescue us!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.62,0:37:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,General Pei, do you have a letter from Commander Xiahou?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:50.62,0:37:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweat has soaked this letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:05.62,0:38:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The letter from Commander Xiahou is hard to read now.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.94,0:38:13.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:13.66,0:38:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I risked my life to deliver this.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.66,0:38:18.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Please do not delay, sir, and send troops now!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.66,0:38:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If Nan'an falls and the Prince Consort Xiahou is hurt, he would blame us.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.18,0:38:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Who could bear this responsibility?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.02,0:38:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.66,0:38:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not send troops, I would rather risk my life to return...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.58,0:38:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,...to report back to Commander Xiahou!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.66,0:38:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,General Pei, stay!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.82,0:38:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Assemble the troops and sally forth to Nan'an.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:47.34,0:38:49.34,Default,,0,0,0,,-Rescue Commander Xiahou!\N-Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.50,0:38:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir! Guan Xing is blocking the front, and Zhang Bao is attacking from behind!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.50,0:39:00.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.26,0:39:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,An ambush! Order all troops to retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.90,0:39:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.46,0:39:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:21.14,0:39:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Administrator Cui is here, lower the drawbridge!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:25.86,0:39:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Cui Liang!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.06,0:39:30.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(950,459)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.86,0:39:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I have taken this city!\N Why not dismount and surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.34,0:39:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Go to Tianshui Commandery!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:06.54,0:40:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Administrator Cui, you have no way to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.38,0:40:11.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not surrender now?
Comment: 0,0:24:23.02,0:24:28.74,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{blur3\\i1}The Analects{\i0} 13:5, translation by James Legge.

